{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nv2wRpKeJ6HbmHyzEh39de","type":"tool_result","content":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/method.tex-21-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/method.tex-22-The window formulation offers two advantages over alternatives.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/method.tex-23-Compared to step-level scoring, windows capture short-range temporal patterns---such as a sequence of repeated failed attempts---that individual actions cannot express.\ndocs/paper/sections/method.tex:24:Compared to trajectory-level labeling, windows provide the granularity needed to pinpoint \\emph{when} stagnation begins and ends within a single task attempt, enabling downstream interventions such as early termination or strategy switching.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/method.tex-25-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/method.tex-26-%-------------------------------------------------------------------\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/method.tex-27-\\subsection{Weak Supervision Pipeline}\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/limitations.tex-12-Three LFs produce insufficient inter-LF conflict (95.1\\% agreement at conf${\\geq}$2) for any label model---temporal or generative---to demonstrate value; scaling to ${>}$10 LFs with higher disagreement is needed.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/limitations.tex-13-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/limitations.tex-14-\\paragraph{No online evaluation.}\ndocs/paper/sections/limitations.tex:15:All results are offline; no intervention or real-time deployment evaluation has been conducted.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/limitations.tex-16-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/limitations.tex-17-\\paragraph{Label version sensitivity.}\ndocs/paper/sections/limitations.tex-18-Cross-coding-agent transfer results are sensitive to label quality: a single embedding version mismatch shifted the OH stagnation rate from 6.56\\% to 21.4\\% and improved 5\\% fine-tuning F1 from 0.570 to 0.850.\n--\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-20-Using a weak supervision framework \\citep{ratner2016dataprogramming,ratner2019snorkel}, we construct silver-labeled datasets from over 205K windows spanning SWE-Agent (54,809 windows, 28.5\\% silver-labeled stagnation) and OpenHands (150,652 windows, 20.9\\% stagnation).\ndocs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-21-Three labeling functions provide complementary noisy votes: command repetition ($\\lambda_1$) targets repetitive behavior, file diff delta ($\\lambda_2$) targets output productivity, and outcome backpropagation ($\\lambda_3$) propagates task-level outcomes backward through the trajectory.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-22-Majority vote aggregation produces window-level binary labels with confidence scores.\ndocs/paper/sections/introduction.tex:23:Our window-level formulation ($k{=}5$ consecutive actions, stride 1) captures short-range temporal patterns---such as repeated failures followed by strategy changes---that step-level approaches cannot express, while providing the granularity to pinpoint \\emph{when} stagnation begins and ends within a trajectory, enabling targeted interventions.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-24-Against these silver labels, we systematically compare hand-crafted structural features, a neural embedding probe, and an LLM-as-judge baseline.\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-25-\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/docs/paper/sections/introduction.tex-26-Our study yields three principal findings."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014d2sdmLz88YrxkF9TCz64H","session_id":"8ba2873e-73c0-42d5-b773-116ccfe0b545","uuid":"613d801d-a185-4ea1-98c2-4764e1791e10","timestamp":"2026-05-16T03:21:09.454Z"}
